#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050644 :topic/difficulty 1.0054125078076268 :topic/id #uuid "5beaefa1-1d02-51a5-90bc-250adca28a57" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092382 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091951 :question/id #uuid "2f5afc63-6988-5676-b170-5826e659a5fd" :question/math-academy-id "e-144" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y = 2x^3 - 2x$ at the point $(1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x) = 2x^3 - 2x.$ Computing the derivative $f'(x)$ gives\n\n$$\nf'(x)  = 6x^2-2.\n$$\n\nWe then compute $f'(1)$, which gives\n\n$$\nf'(1)  = 6(1)^2-2 = 4.\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the point-slope form with $m=4$ and the coordinates of our point $(1,0),$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-0 & =4(x-1) \\\\ y & =4x-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "db808f48-6d0c-5b35-9342-b1817df65172" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Line to a Curve at a Point"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092383 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091952 :question/id #uuid "e248bb90-ba83-5e3f-938b-2c8be7d6eb7a" :question/math-academy-id "e-146" :question/problem "Find where the tangent to the curve $y=4\\sqrt{x}+4x$ at the point $(1,8)$ intersects the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=4\\sqrt{x}+4x.$ Let's first calculate the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\sqrt{x}+4x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{x}^{1/2}+4x) \\\\  & =2{x}^{-1/2}+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the slope of the tangent at our point is\n\n$$\nm=f'(1) = 2(1)^{-1/2}+4 = 6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the tangent is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-8 & =6(x-1) \\\\ y & =6x-6+8 \\\\ y & =6x+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the tangent line intercepts the $x$-axis, we set $y=0$ and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =6x+2 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is $\\left(-\\dfrac 1 3, 0\\right).$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c8ba29-95c9-5494-be0b-9b67bee6e45c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining where a Tangent Line Intersects an Axis"}] :topic/math-academy-id 986 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049119} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049248} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050420} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051084}] :topic/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Line Using Differentiation"}]}
